fascinating study conducted by researchers Alesina, Cozzi, and Mantovan.

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:14,240
The goal is to explore a fundamental dynamic of our society and try to answer

4
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:19,080
one of perhaps the oldest questions in the world: is wealth truly deserved?

5
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:23,120
In the course of this analysis, we will immerse ourselves in the macroeconomic mechanisms proposed by these

6
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:27,679
scholars, and it is incredible to note how human beliefs about what is right or wrong are not

7
00:00:27,679 --> 00:00:32,640
just abstract thoughts, but literally shape over the long term the economic destiny,

8
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:36,119
fiscal policies, and growth of entire nations.

9
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:41,920
And it is precisely by looking at the global landscape that a crucial question arises; people often

10
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:46,799
wonder why apparently identical societies end up choosing diametrically opposed

11
00:00:46,799 --> 00:00:52,399
economic paths and fiscal policies. In short, if two nations start with exactly

12
